<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's KFA passes on 140,000T soymeal tenders.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's KFA passes on 140,000T soymeal tenders.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Korea Feed Association (KFA) on Thursday passed on tenders for 140,000 tonnes of soymeal due to high offer prices, traders said.</p>
<p>Officials with KFA were not immediately available for comment. </p>
<p>Traders said the offer prices were much higher than expected due to a sharp gain on the Chicago Board of Trade on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Details for the passed tenders are as follows:</p>
<p>  POSITION  TONNE    ETA	  ARRIVAL PORT</p>
<p>  One     30,000   May 30     Inchon</p>
<p>  Two     30,000   May 20     Ulsan/Kunsan</p>
<p>  Three   30,000   June 30    Inchon</p>
<p>  Four    50,000   June 20    Inchon/Kunsan</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
